# XGen Protocol — git line-ending policy.
#
# core.autocrlf=true otherwise wants CRLF in the working tree, so cargo/tauri
# rewriting the workspace manifests as LF on every build re-flags them as
# modified in `git status` (no content change — pure line-ending churn).
# Pinning Cargo manifests to LF overrides autocrlf for just these files and
# stops the churn. (J-410 follow-up; manifests are already LF, so no
# renormalization.) The basename pattern matches Cargo.toml in every crate.
Cargo.toml text eol=lf
